description:
Owning bead: eshyra-o9bd.19.6.3. Read its description, ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA and every note; the 2026-09-22 and 2026-10-09 rebaselines are operative. Authority: ADR 0020 and section 5.9 of docs/audits/rules-awareness-transition/2026-07-30-integrated-transition-design.md (the nine-condition bar; see section 13.3 and R4: a gate that recognizes nothing has FAILED TO RUN, it has not passed).

THIS CHILD BUILDS THE GATES; it does not certify the candidate. The supervisor runs the bundle at the candidate commit after integration. Do not edit the finding registry, the audit docs under docs/audits/dnd5e-srd-5.1-final/, or pack/importer files (another child owns those).

ROOT CAUSE: packages/core/scripts/create-dnd5e-srd-audit-bundle/cli.ts captures command outputs and many reports, but:
 - it never fails when a captured command exits non-zero. It only logs the exit code;
 - no report states its bounded denominator or what it does not observe;
 - nothing checks re-freeze bar #5 (every registry finding dispositioned) or AC3/AC4 evidence presence;
 - the bundle README carries no candidate identity beyond commit and branch, and no explicit non-claims.

REQUIRED:
1. A typed gate model in that script (or a sibling module in the same directory): `{ id, observes: string, doesNotObserve: string[], denominator: { description: string, count: number }, result: 'pass' | 'fail' | 'failed-to-run', details: string[] }`. A gate whose denominator count is 0 is 'failed-to-run', never 'pass'. Emit reports/candidate-gates.json and reports/candidate-gates.txt.
2. The bundle process exits non-zero if any gate is not 'pass'. It must still write every report first, so the reviewer can see why.
3. Gates (each states observes / doesNotObserve in-band):
   G-repro: `verify:dnd5e-srd-pack` captured exit code is 0. The denominator is the pack artifacts that the verifier compares; read them from the verifier's own list, not a copied number.
   G-source-hash: the vendored PDF sha256 equals packages/core/sources/dnd5e-srd-5.1/manifest.json and the pack manifest's recorded source hash. Reuse verifySourceHash.
   G-suite: the `check`, `typecheck` and `test` captured exit codes are all 0.
   G-registry (bar #5): load docs/audits/dnd5e-srd-5.1-final/finding-registry.json through the existing findingRegistry loader (packages/core/src/rules/findingRegistry.ts), which validates the contract. Every row has a status, every non-accepted row has statusReasoning, and every alias resolves. Denominator: the row count. doesNotObserve must state:
     - whether the pack currently violates any row (registry non-claim);
     - live bead state.
   G-finding-evidence (AC3): for every registry statusReasoning, extract each cited repository path (e.g. `packages/core/test/...test.ts`). Every path must exist, and every cited test file must be part of the G-suite run (it lives under the vitest include globs; reuse vitest.config.ts include patterns, do not hand-copy them). Denominator: cited paths. Rows whose reasoning cites no path are listed in details as 'no committed evidence pointer'. That is NOT a failure. State it in doesNotObserve as 'whether each pointer discriminates the defect (eshyra-o9bd.19.1.8 owns that)'.
   G-capabilities (AC4): for every DETERMINISTIC_CAPABILITY_INVENTORY entry (packages/core/src/rules/deterministicCapabilityInventory.ts) and every RULE_DETERMINISTIC_CAPABILITY_CONTRACTS entry (deterministicCapabilityLedger.ts), every runtimeOwner and evidence path exists, and every evidence test is inside the G-suite run. Denominator: entries. doesNotObserve: the absence of a binding is not a completeness result; the unselected magic-item backlog is not covered; semantic correctness of each capability is not covered, beyond its tests passing in G-suite.
   G-replay (replay/deterministic equivalence, where applicable): the pack replay is G-repro. For capabilities, list the inventory entries whose contract or operation text declares seeded dice ('seed'/'seeded'), and require that each cites at least one evidence test. Denominator: those entries. If none match, the gate is failed-to-run, not pass. Read the inventory first; if the honest predicate differs, choose the narrowest truthful one and explain it in the report.
4. Bundle README (buildReadme):
   - candidate identity: commit, source PDF sha256, and the sha256 of every pack artifact copied into the bundle;
   - a gate summary table;
   - an 'Explicit non-claims' section: no universal clause, mechanic, deterministic or discovery completeness; passing authorizes independent audit (eshyra-o9bd.16), not re-freeze;
   - an 'Unresolved limits disclosed' section that points to docs/audits/dnd5e-srd-5.1-final/2026-11-01-o9bd-19-6-1-candidate-pack.md (being written by a sibling; reference it by path, and fail the gate run if the file is absent at bundle time: G-candidate-record). It must name eshyra-o9bd.19.3.5's bounded discovery limitation explicitly, per the 2026-10-09 note.
5. Keep existing reports and behaviour. Do not weaken dnd5eSrdAuditBundle.test.ts. Add focused unit tests there (or beside it) for the gate model:
   - a zero-denominator gate is failed-to-run;
   - any non-pass gate makes the overall result fail;
   - G-registry fails on a malformed or unreasoned non-accepted row;
   - G-finding-evidence and G-capabilities fail on a missing path;
   - G-replay with no matching entries is failed-to-run.
   Test the pure functions; do not run the whole bundle in tests.

ENGINE BOUNDARY: tooling only, no runtime change.
COMPLETION PROOF: `npm run verify:worktree` passes; the commit is on the assigned branch only. Report:
 - each gate's predicate as implemented;
 - the G-replay predicate you chose, with its matching entries;
 - every place you deviated from this spec, and why.
Do NOT run the full bundle (it is slow and copies to /mnt/d by default). If you sanity-run it, pass explicit args: `npm run audit-bundle:dnd5e-srd -- <scratch-dir> <scratch-zip>`, both outside the repo.
